      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Carroll Park, the third landscape park in Baltimore, sits within Pigtown and offers baseball, football, and a skate park.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pigtown%2C_Baltimore",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Pigtown’s boundaries run from Martin Luther King Boulevard and Barre Circle eastward to Pratt St north, Carey St west, and the Carroll Camden Industrial area south.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://swpbal.org/pigtown/",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The neighborhood’s German heritage flourished after 1868 when the B&O partnered with the North-German Lloyd Steamship Company, boosting local industry.",
